#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407163 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152094 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "051e28ef-ac7f-5b29-bd93-c1e24a4bc699" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Free and Bound Occurrences of Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2108dc3f-8bf7-5722-88d5-6553aea7bf61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407146} {:answer/id #uuid "2ab77857-2df1-5afa-b593-651b139d8699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407148} {:answer/id #uuid "a1c2ef64-ac61-56b4-a3f5-211311616d33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407152} {:answer/id #uuid "b6153063-5e62-52e4-9bee-993b29720aee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407154} {:answer/id #uuid "fb316e3c-6f70-5a11-be3f-2488818c1837" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ab77857-2df1-5afa-b593-651b139d8699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407148} :answer-field/id #uuid "68d7f5e7-3696-5415-aa0d-dffd949f398d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407160}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "085a10d3-7324-5921-95c5-eaa8f395984a" :question/math-academy-id "q-183620" :question/problem "$$\n∀{k}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{I}\\end{aligned}}\\in (0,1),\\,{n}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{II}\\end{aligned}}+{k}^{2}\\ge {k}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{III}\\end{aligned}}\n$$\n\nWhich occurrences of the variables in the expression above are free?" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our expression and mark the occurrences of the variables as bound $(\\text{b})$ or free $(\\text{f}).$\n\n- Occurrence I of the variable $k$ is *bound* since it's placed right next to the quantifier $∀:$\n\n$$\n∀{k}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in (0,1),\\,n+{k}^{2}\\ge k\n$$\n\n- Occurrence II of the variable $n$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $n.$\n\n- Occurrence III of the variable $k$ is *bound* since it lies within the scope of the quantifier $∀k$ that uses $k:$\n\n$$\n∀k\\in (0,1),\\,\\overset{\\text{scope of }∀k}{\\overset{⏞}{n+{k}^{2}\\ge {k}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}}}\n$$\n\nThe occurrences of variables in the expression are as follows:\n\n$$\n∀\\,{k}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in (0,1),\\,{n}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}+{k}^{2}\\ge {k}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the free occurrence is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407165 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152094 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "051e28ef-ac7f-5b29-bd93-c1e24a4bc699" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Free and Bound Occurrences of Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1943552a-2f42-5c04-b2b2-141962e83629" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407145} {:answer/id #uuid "2362167e-158f-5ff6-98a3-0b706701da84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407147} {:answer/id #uuid "321d0d48-cf92-590c-b6d4-e7a9c6d3ddbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407149} {:answer/id #uuid "bfee88a5-cc20-5302-a89d-798128cc26a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407155} {:answer/id #uuid "f6c05a0d-3046-5d14-b8a4-1703eef736d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2362167e-158f-5ff6-98a3-0b706701da84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407147} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3f68dc1-1788-54d0-8ac8-3e61f521a037" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407162}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "39d9d2c3-0d6e-5d14-b069-fbe9f014d46f" :question/math-academy-id "q-183674" :question/problem "$$\n(\\,∀{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{I}\\end{aligned}}\\in R,\\,0<x<1\\,)⇒(\\,∃y\\in R,\\,{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{II}\\end{aligned}}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{III}\\end{aligned}}\\,)\n$$\n\nWhich occurrences of the variables in the expression above are free?" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our expression and mark the occurrences of the variables as bound $(\\text{b})$ or free $(\\text{f}).$\n\n- Occurrence I of the variable $x$ is *bound* since it is placed right next to the quantifier $∀:$\n\n$$\n(\\,∀{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in R,\\,0<x<1\\,)⇒(\\,∃y\\in R,\\,x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,)\n$$\n\n- Occurrence II of the variable $x$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $x.$\n\n- Occurrence III of the variable $y$ is *bound* since it lies within the scope of the quantifier $∃y$ that uses $y:$\n\n$$\n(\\,∀x\\in R,\\,0<x<1\\,)⇒(\\,∃y\\in R,\\,\\overset{\\text{scope of }∃y}{\\overset{⏞}{x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}}})\n$$\n\nThe occurrences of variables in the expression are as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\,∀{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in R,\\,0<{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}<1\\,)⇒(\\,∃{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in R,\\,{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\,)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the free occurrence is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407164 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152095 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6927f03c-aa7a-56ac-8cd0-c036a11aadc9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Value of a Statement Involving Nested Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "323a480f-fb01-5766-92ab-c2eb831689ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407150} {:answer/id #uuid "6c8dd577-5b41-5386-91e2-6d8dadf4331d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407151} {:answer/id #uuid "abae491e-3dfc-5abb-b6f5-dc7f6456e165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407153} {:answer/id #uuid "ca49dde2-0454-5f89-bafe-f932d21ec499" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407156} {:answer/id #uuid "e4be5bf2-f7c6-557b-967a-fefc572c2364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4be5bf2-f7c6-557b-967a-fefc572c2364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407157} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0f1732b-6bd9-5f1d-9035-c362872ddd7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407161}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0a806540-0634-5e11-9ba2-ff988650a653" :question/math-academy-id "q-183877" :question/problem "Let $p\\in Q$ and $q\\in Q.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $∃\\,p\\in Q,\\,2p=-1.$\n- The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∃\\,p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot q=-1\\,)$ is $Q.$\n- $∃\\,q,p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot q=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the statement \n\n$$\n∃\\,q,p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot q=-1\n$$\n\nfrom option III reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ There exist rationals $q$ and $p,$ such that $p\\cdot q=-1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true, $2p=-1$ for some rational number $p$ (e.g., for $p=-\\frac{1}{2}$).\n\n- Statement II is false. For the predicate\n\n$$\nP(q):\\,∃\\,p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot q=-1\n$$\n\nwe note that $P(q)$ is true for some $q\\in Q$ and false for others. For example, \n\n$$\nP(0):\\,∃\\,p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot 0=-1\n$$\n\nis false. However, \n\n$$\nP(1):\\,∃\\,p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot 1=-1\n$$\n\nis true, since we can take $p=-1.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The sentence \n\n$$\n(\\,∃\\,q,p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot q=-1\\,)\n$$\n\n \ncan be written as\n\n$$\n∃q\\in Q\\,(\\,{{∃p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot q=-1}_{⏟}}_{P(q)}\\,)\n$$\n\nwhich is true whenever the inner predicate $P(q)$ has a nonempty truth set. And according to the discussion in statement II, this is the case.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}]}
